import Hedgehog
import Support
import EthLib.Consensus.Preset
import EthLib.Consensus.Config

/-!
# Presets and configurations by the names of their values

A preset or a configuration is a general parameter of the functions of the consensus layer.

So a test draws one, and both sides must build the same one from its words.

A word is `NAME=value`, and the value replaces that of a named preset or configuration.

This file is the table of the names, one line for each field of the two structures.
-/

open EthLib EthLib.Consensus

namespace ProtocolsProperty

/-- A preset with one value replaced, by the name of the value in consensus-specs.

A name that the preset does not have leaves it as it was. -/
